WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.298
[...]

00:00:04.298 --> 00:00:09.651
SPEAKER 1: Casey Martin was a
professional golfer with a bad leg.

00:00:09.651 --> 00:00:15.541
Due to a circulatory disorder, walking
the course for 18 holes of golf

00:00:15.545 --> 00:00:17.492
was painful for Martin.

00:00:17.492 --> 00:00:22.445
It even posed a serious risk
that he might fracture his leg.

00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:26.851
Despite this disability,
he was an excellent golfer.

00:00:26.851 --> 00:00:31.181
He asked the PGA, the
Professional Golfers' Association,

00:00:31.181 --> 00:00:35.789
for permission to use a golf
cart during the tournaments.

00:00:35.789 --> 00:00:38.637
The PGA said no.

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:41.669
Martin took his case to court.

00:00:41.669 --> 00:00:44.947
He invoked a law requiring
that organizations

00:00:44.947 --> 00:00:49.366
make reasonable accommodations
for people with disabilities

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:52.450
provided the accommodation
did not fundamentally

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.985
alter the nature of the activity.

00:00:55.985 --> 00:01:00.385
Many of the great golfers of
the past testified in court

00:01:00.389 --> 00:01:04.809
that walking the course was
an essential part of the game.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.948
The case went all the way
to the US Supreme Court.

00:01:08.948 --> 00:01:10.924
The Court ruled in Martin's favor.

00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:14.994
They said he did have a right to
use a golf cart in the tournaments.

00:01:15.011 --> 00:01:18.292
The Court ruled that the
essence of golf was the ability

00:01:18.292 --> 00:01:23.632
to make shots, not the
ability to walk the course.

00:01:23.636 --> 00:01:27.726
Critics argued that giving
Martin a right to ride in a golf

00:01:27.726 --> 00:01:30.656
cart while competing in
professional tournaments

00:01:30.669 --> 00:01:33.685
would be like giving a
disabled basketball player

00:01:33.685 --> 00:01:36.055
who was a great shooter
the right to play

00:01:36.055 --> 00:01:41.385
in the NBA while riding up and down
the court in a motorized scooter.

00:01:41.389 --> 00:01:42.997
What do you think?

00:01:42.997 --> 00:01:45.437
Do you agree with the
reasoning of the court

00:01:45.457 --> 00:01:49.597
or with the reasoning of the critics?

